            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Well, the \"bump\" commit _replaced_ the 1.17 tarball with the 1.19 tarball, which was stupid of me. Adding and removing tarballs should be independent actions. (We need to keep dependencies cached as long as we support building versions that use that version.)\r\n\r\n(Actually, I shouldn't have touched this at all; the GNU deps are not worth chasing; I just got triggered by the version discrepancy between CMake and Zig.)",
